{"id": "EUVD-2026-27686", "enisaUuid": "8f21e40e-3f4e-3c73-b6b7-08ebd4ff32bb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: fix circular locking dependency in run_unpack_ex\n\nSyzbot reported a circular locking dependency between wnd->rw_lock\n(sbi->used.bitmap) and ni->file.run_lock.\n\nThe deadlock scenario:\n1. ntfs_extend_mft() takes ni->file.run_lock then wnd->rw_lock.\n2. run_unpack_ex() takes wnd->rw_lock then tries to acquire\n   ni->file.run_lock inside ntfs_refresh_zone().\n\nThis creates an AB-BA deadlock.\n\nFix this by using down_read_trylock() instead of down_read() when\nacquiring run_lock in run_unpack_ex(). If the lock is contended,\nskip ntfs_refresh_zone() - the MFT zone will be refreshed on the\nnext MFT operation. This breaks the circular dependency since we\nnever block waiting for run_lock while holding wnd->rw_lock.", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T11:27:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d60f09d2d16c44a797d8cb67015cde2508720506", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76016d15bbd90caa0ce7765fddf9bde8e943e601", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b014372b62237521444ee51384549bdf48b79015", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8d22d9d8260b0f4f4d8e2898c98037c9982ea66", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08ce2fee1b869ecbfbd94e0eb2630e52203a2e03"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43127", "GHSA-pmpx-w3f2-x2vp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05986165-84d3-3d17-a980-de22664c24b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.66 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "064523cd-a7ad-3458-ae74-0c0da32d6fac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db7fc56646cafe39599a4c21f1398e2bdfd5c185 <76016d15bbd90caa0ce7765fddf9bde8e943e601"}, {"id": "0ae9cc6c-6300-34a2-a0e8-27da08b8aa1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fc982fe7eca9d0cf7b25832450ebd4f7c8e1c36 <b014372b62237521444ee51384549bdf48b79015"}, {"id": "308639db-dce1-35bf-9dca-d5566c6e2a07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "54c8b00d-f7b6-3538-b8be-6bfff867009e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fc982fe7eca9d0cf7b25832450ebd4f7c8e1c36 <b8d22d9d8260b0f4f4d8e2898c98037c9982ea66"}, {"id": "6c8a5990-a2c4-39b3-b7c0-09bbf1ef7c96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "71025068-d744-3eef-8752-8494f8d8ba90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "57f7979aefdcef66326bda47e07ee0d8be64bf21 <d60f09d2d16c44a797d8cb67015cde2508720506"}, {"id": "a8ee8154-cb7a-34fd-a5d9-95edc3ecc9b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.5 <6.12.114"}, {"id": "b4834c0d-f593-3d8e-af31-2539b1f684f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "e46a1c84-082e-3e91-a388-d0a87a44ed11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.16"}, {"id": "ea5cb455-e96f-368f-bc55-63431d098cc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fc982fe7eca9d0cf7b25832450ebd4f7c8e1c36 <08ce2fee1b869ecbfbd94e0eb2630e52203a2e03"}, {"id": "f10791a4-1d26-3892-b3f0-897dfcd4ae20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "f5509b69-8187-3591-b266-be8d9b1aecab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "f884fac5-eb2b-353a-9404-795264dfe93e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2ec059fa-1f5f-3ff8-9832-62663b7400c5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}